WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:03.740
Let's go instead to our caller from the 9
7 2 area code.

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:06.569
Who's calling from 9 7 to.

00:00:06.569 --> 00:00:09.480
By David is Daniel from Texas, Zoe Daniel,
what's going on?

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.660
I have a question for you.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:13.469
So I'm a big advocate of Medicare for all.

00:00:13.469 --> 00:00:19.250
Like many of your listeners and yourself,
one of the questions that come up from our

00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:27.070
friends and family is should it be included
in a Medicare for all option or whatever plan

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:34.589
we come up with that we are including all
of the insurance employees as part of retraining

00:00:34.589 --> 00:00:39.610
or even bringing them onto a government ran
system?

00:00:39.610 --> 00:00:44.469
Or should it be included in the budgeting
for that or how would you picture that?

00:00:44.469 --> 00:00:48.910
A the Democratic Party, since they'll be the
ones that end up pushing it through, how do

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:52.640
you plan that they will do it versus how do
you think it should be done to incorporate

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:54.180
all those people who lose their jobs?

00:00:54.180 --> 00:00:55.180
Well, here's the thing.

00:00:55.180 --> 00:01:00.399
A lot of the people that work in the health
insurance industry don't really need to be

00:01:00.399 --> 00:01:02.410
retrained in this.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.500
They're going to need to find new jobs for
sure.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.450
But it's not really the training piece that
they need help with.

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:12.070
What I mean by that is so everyone who's as
a service provider would just continue like

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.700
if you're a doctor, you stay a doctor.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.020
If you're a nurse, you stay indoors.

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.020
Okay.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:19.870
Executive level people, human resources people,
you know, all of these people that work at

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:26.360
health insurance companies there, their skills
would still be in demand, as is at other companies.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.460
We would just need to find other companies
for them.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.160
So certainly that would be a piece of it.

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:37.750
There's really only a slice of healthcare
company employees that would really need retraining.

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:43.110
I mean, OK, maybe you don't need nearly as
many medical billing people and that's a really

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:46.000
specific narrow job that would be less relevant.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:49.890
You'll still need some of them because remember,
single payer still involves billing.

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:51.640
It's just that there's one payer.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.660
So I actually don't know that retraining is
really the thing.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:02:00.159
I think it's going to be more a jobs program
to figure out where are they going to go?

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:03.620
Do they get involved in government infrastructure
programs?

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:06.020
Do we transition them over to green energy?

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:07.650
Stuff like that is a question.

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:11.720
I don't know that retraining is really the
issue.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.130
I agree and I agree with that.

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.561
I just kind of wanted to set the stage there
for your thoughts on it.

00:02:16.561 --> 00:02:20.750
And do you think do you think that the numbers.

00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.100
Should be included in any budget.

00:02:22.100 --> 00:02:28.440
So we have debates or discussions about that
regarding the cost of that.

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:33.450
Or do you see it already shown in those numbers?

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:36.520
I don't know the answer as to whether it's
already in the numbers.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:37.580
I just simply don't know.

00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:40.600
God, in my belief, because I want to be transparent
is.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:41.600
Yeah.

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.530
If we think about what it's going to cost
to do Medicare for all, I want to include

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:45.800
in that.

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:51.360
Whatever costs we are including to transition
a lot of the people that will lose their jobs

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.600
over to Newt.

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:53.600
I would include that.

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:59.240
Now Republicans in bad faith would simply
say, oh, so it costs even more than you said,

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:00.240
right.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.240
I mean so but so.

00:03:01.240 --> 00:03:03.730
So for political reasons, maybe it's best
not to include it.

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:07.160
But if I really want to holistically think
about what's the total cost here, I would

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:11.940
include the transition costs for how the government
will support healthcare company employees

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:13.880
moving elsewhere.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.680
Great, thank you.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:16.680
Have a good one.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:17.680
All right.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:18.680
Appreciate the call.

00:03:18.680 --> 00:03:19.680
Thank you so much.

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:20.680
OK.

00:03:20.680 --> 00:03:23.390
I don't have time to take more calls today,
but I will take calls again.

00:03:23.390 --> 00:03:25.690
And I really appreciate everybody who called
in.

00:03:25.690 --> 00:03:27.930
Hope to hear from you very, very soon.

